  "notes": [
    "Single hidden PRODUCT support is recovered with complement group tests; query count <= d(ceil(log2 n)+1)+1.",
    "Binary-oracle information lower bound is ceil(log2 C(n,d)).",
    "For strict-positive eta gates, complement finite-amplitude probes have a depth-independent gap >=1-eta, while local q-jets attenuate as (1-eta)^q eta^(d-q).",
    "For a positive polynomial, Boolean positivity queries identify exactly the upward closure generated by inclusion-minimal monomial supports.",
    "Sign-only Boolean support queries cannot identify nonminimal monomials; richer magnitude/amplitude queries are required."
